---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CaseHero from '../../components/CaseHero.astro';
import CaseNext from '../../components/CaseNext.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Kemp Beauty – Gabriel Alisasis" description="Eight Klaviyo flows showed live. A DMARC policy was silently bouncing almost all of it, and the fix ran deeper than the dashboard.">
  <div class="page-top-spacer" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <section id="case">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="breadcrumb-head">
        <a href="/work">← All work</a>
        <button id="fanTrigger" class="tag" style="cursor:pointer; margin-left:auto;">⛶ Preview screenshots</button>
      </div>
      <CaseHero slug="kemp-beauty" />

      <div class="case-list">
        <article class="case reveal">
          <div class="case-body">
              <div class="pao">
                <div class="pao-col pao-problem">
                  <h4>Problem</h4>
                  <p>Every marketing email was sent from <code>info@kempbeauty.com</code> – a domain with no DKIM keys in Klaviyo and a DMARC policy of <code>p=reject</code>. Gmail refused all of it:</p>
                  <p style="margin-top:9px"><code>550 5.7.26 Unauthenticated email … not accepted due to DMARC policy</code></p>
                  <p style="margin-top:9px">Klaviyo showed all eight flows as live the entire time. <strong>Flow status and actual delivery are two different things</strong>, and nothing in the interface surfaced the gap.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pao-col pao-approach">
                  <h4>Approach</h4>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Audited sending domains and found exactly one verified: <code>mail.kempbeauty.com</code>, DKIM and site-verification records confirmed.</li>
                    <li>Tested authenticating the bare root domain and established it is <strong>impossible, not merely awkward</strong> – CNAME records cannot exist at a zone apex.</li>
                    <li>Rewrote the sender across <strong>26 messages in 8 flows</strong>, including a live A/B test's variations, keeping reply-to on the real inbox.</li>
                    <li>Traced a <strong>second, separate failure</strong>: double opt-in confirmation emails carry their own sender setting that Klaviyo's API doesn't expose – invisible until you test a real signup.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="pao-col pao-outcome">
                  <h4>Outcome</h4>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Verified with a live signup end to end: submit → subscribe → <strong>delivered to Gmail</strong>, zero bounces or drops.</li>
                    <li>Cross-checked against Klaviyo's own reporting rather than trusting the event log alone.</li>
                    <li>Flagged the tradeoff rather than burying it: the <code>mail.</code> subdomain's MX points at Klaviyo, so replies there never reach the team.</li>
                    <li>Recommended staged domain warming instead of resuming full volume on a subdomain with no sending history.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="diagram-wrap">
                <div class="cap">Fig. 03 – why the mail vanished, and the fix</div>
                <svg class="diagram" viewBox="0 0 900 240" role="img"
                     aria-label="Diagram comparing two sending paths. Before: the Klaviyo flow sends from the unauthenticated root domain, fails the DMARC reject policy, and Gmail returns a 550 bounce. After: the flow sends from the DKIM-verified mail subdomain, passes DMARC, and reaches the inbox.">
                  <rect class="dg-box" x="8" y="86" width="140" height="58"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="22" y="110">Klaviyo flow</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="22" y="126">8 flows · 26 messages</text>

                  <text class="dg-head" x="212" y="40">BEFORE</text>
                  <rect class="dg-box" x="212" y="50" width="168" height="52"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="226" y="72">From: kempbeauty.com</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="226" y="88">no DKIM keys</text>

                  <rect class="dg-box" x="424" y="50" width="150" height="52"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="438" y="72">DMARC check</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="438" y="88">p=reject</text>

                  <rect class="dg-box dg-box-neg" x="618" y="50" width="180" height="52"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="632" y="72" style="fill:var(--neg)">550 5.7.26 – bounced</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="632" y="88">never reached the inbox</text>

                  <path class="dg-flow neg" style="--len:70" d="M148 108 L180 108 L180 76 L212 76"/>
                  <path class="dg-flow neg" style="--len:46" d="M380 76 L424 76"/>
                  <path class="dg-flow neg" style="--len:46" d="M574 76 L618 76"/>

                  <text class="dg-head" x="212" y="164">AFTER</text>
                  <rect class="dg-box dg-box-pos" x="212" y="174" width="168" height="52"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="226" y="196">From: mail.kempbeauty…</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="226" y="212">DKIM verified</text>

                  <rect class="dg-box dg-box-pos" x="424" y="174" width="150" height="52"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="438" y="196">DMARC check</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="438" y="212">aligned · passes</text>

                  <rect class="dg-box dg-box-pos" x="618" y="174" width="180" height="52"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="632" y="196">Delivered to inbox</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="632" y="212">verified on a live signup</text>

                  <path class="dg-flow pos" style="--len:70" d="M148 122 L180 122 L180 200 L212 200"/>
                  <path class="dg-flow pos" style="--len:46" d="M380 200 L424 200"/>
                  <path class="dg-flow pos" style="--len:46" d="M574 200 L618 200"/>
                </svg>
              </div>

              <h4 class="sub-head">Storefront work</h4>
              <div class="pao" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; margin-bottom:0;">
                <div class="pao-col">
                  <ul>
                    <li>Rebuilt the product page: descriptor above the swatches, spec rows with pipe dividers, dual descriptor cards for two-style packs.</li>
                    <li>Gated add-to-cart when a 2-pack is selected with fewer than two styles chosen – a real source of broken orders.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="pao-col">
                  <ul>
                    <li>Replaced stock-photo testimonials with real Loox reviews, and rebuilt the About page for visual cohesion.</li>
                    <li>Fixed a site-wide bug where product cards went blank on hover.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="stack-row">
                <span class="pill">Klaviyo</span><span class="pill">Shopify Liquid</span><span class="pill">DNS · DKIM · DMARC</span>
                <span class="pill">Loox</span><span class="pill">Git</span><span class="pill">GraphQL Admin API</span>
              </div>

              <figure class="case-gallery">
                <img class="zoomable" src="/images/work/kemp-beauty-pdp.webp" width="1200" height="750" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                     alt="Kemp Beauty product page for Press On Performance Lash Strips showing the style descriptor card above the swatch row and one-pack and two-pack options">
                <figcaption>The rebuilt product page – the descriptor card sits above the swatches so the style name and its copy read as one unit before you pick.</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
          
        </article>

      </div>
      <CaseNext slug="kemp-beauty" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
